From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] zstd: avoid the bit-mask table load on C906

Use the existing shift-based bit reader on XTheadBb RV64. It handles
zero-width reads without a dependent load from the bit-mask table.
XTheadBb is a compile-time proxy for NanoKVM's C906 tuning profile, not
a requirement of this shift sequence. Other XTheadBb RV64 cores use the
same mathematically equivalent path; performance has only been measured
on C906.

Signed-off-by: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/lib/zstd/common/bitstream.h b/lib/zstd/common/bitstream.h
--- a/lib/zstd/common/bitstream.h
+++ b/lib/zstd/common/bitstream.h
@@ -315,12 +315,15 @@
 FORCE_INLINE_TEMPLATE BitContainerType BIT_lookBits(const BIT_DStream_t*  bitD, U32 nbBits)
 {
     /* arbitrate between double-shift and shift+mask */
-#if 1
+#if !defined(__riscv_xtheadbb) || __riscv_xlen != 64
     /* if bitD->bitsConsumed + nbBits > sizeof(bitD->bitContainer)*8,
      * bitstream is likely corrupted, and result is undefined */
     return BIT_getMiddleBits(bitD->bitContainer, (sizeof(bitD->bitContainer)*8) - bitD->bitsConsumed - nbBits, nbBits);
 #else
-    /* this code path is slower on my os-x laptop */
+    /* XTheadBb selects our C906 tuning profile, not an instruction need.
+     * This also selects other XTheadBb RV64 cores; only C906 is measured.
+     * Avoid the dependent mask load, including for nbBits == 0.
+     */
     U32 const regMask = sizeof(bitD->bitContainer)*8 - 1;
     return ((bitD->bitContainer << (bitD->bitsConsumed & regMask)) >> 1) >> ((regMask-nbBits) & regMask);
 #endif
